35,2,1,talk,Mio,,I found out that some rooms are way colder than others! It's not fair to split equally if some of us are freezing just to save money.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The statements show extreme volatility. The winter bills are nearly triple the summer ones. This makes a flat monthly budget impossible without a large reserve.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Guys, I looked into the ""easy"" ways, and they aren't easy! The templates and other houses' methods take forever. It's like a part-time job just to pay the gas!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,My findings confirm the suspicion. One person is using four times the electricity of another. A flat split is effectively a subsidy for the heaviest user.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The payment logs show that late payments always follow a dispute over the amount. We aren't just fighting about money; we're fighting about the lack of transparency.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, that's a huge difference! But if we track every single watt, will we all just be terrified to turn on a lamp? That sounds so stressful.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"We must also consider the cost of precision. Installing sub-meters would cost us over 170,000 yen total. That is an unacceptable upfront expense for this house.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Exactly! And the ""settling up"" process I saw took forty minutes every single month! Who wants to spend their free time doing that? It's boring and annoying!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Stress is a byproduct of unfairness, Mio. The current ""simplicity"" is just a mask for the fact that some of us are paying for others' luxury.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"If we go for extreme precision, we might just create more points of conflict. Every single kilowatt becomes a potential argument. We need a middle ground.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I just want us to be able to be warm in February without feeling guilty! Can't we just have a ""comfort allowance"" that everyone gets?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A comfort allowance is a good idea, but it doesn't solve the volatility. We need a system that smooths out the winter spikes without costing us a fortune now.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm telling you, if the system is too complicated, the person in charge will just quit or get grumpy. We need something that takes five minutes, not forty!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A ""comfort allowance"" is just a flat split with a different name. If the usage gap is 4:1, the math doesn't change. We need a usage-based tier.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, the problem isn't just the math. It's that the person asking for money is seen as the ""bad guy."" We need a system that feels automatic and impersonal.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm really worried that if we focus only on the ""4:1"" gap, we'll forget that some rooms are just naturally colder. That's not the user's fault!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree with Mio. We cannot ignore the structural differences of the rooms. However, we cannot afford the electrician's quote. We need a software or policy solution.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"Please, let's just pick the one that requires the least amount of typing! I can't stand the thought of someone spending their whole evening on a spreadsheet.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Structural differences are a variable, but they don't explain a 400% difference. Let's stop making excuses for inefficiency and start valuing actual consumption.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"Let's look at the options. We need to balance the ""fairness"" Shunichi wants with the ""simplicity"" Rin wants, and the ""peace"" I want.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
