60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I like Option A! It gives us a predictable cost, so we don't have to panic every time we turn on the heater, but it still settles up eventually.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option B is financially unfeasible due to the installation costs I found. Option C is too volatile; the winter spikes would be a shock to everyone's budget.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option C is the fastest to calculate, but Option A sounds okay too. As long as the ""end of year"" settle isn't a giant nightmare of a spreadsheet!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C is an insult to those of us who are mindful of our usage. Option B is the only truly fair one, but if the cost is too high, Option A is the only rational compromise.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B would create a permanent record of ""who uses more,"" which could lead to more judgment. Option A removes the monthly friction and makes the settle a rare event.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, if you agree Option A is a compromise, then let's go for it! It means we can all be warm without feeling like we're stealing from each other.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A provides the predictability I need. By smoothing the costs over the year, we avoid the ""second rent"" feeling in winter without spending 170,000 yen on meters.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, if we do Option A, who does the end-of-year math? If it's just one big job once a year, I can handle that better than a monthly chore!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"It's not perfect, but it's better than the current chaos. It acknowledges the seasonal nature of the bills while preventing the monthly ""who is carrying whom"" arguments.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"Option A is the best for the house's atmosphere. It stops the monthly reminders from becoming weapons and moves the financial discussion to a scheduled, single event.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm so glad we're agreeing! I can finally stop wearing my coat in the living room and just enjoy the house with everyone.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I will support Option A. It is the most reasonable balance between upfront cost, monthly stability, and long-term accuracy.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for A! One big cleanup a year is way better than a monthly headache. Let's just make sure we use a simple list for it!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll vote for A, provided we are honest about the seasonal rates. We can't set them too low, or the year-end settle will be a disaster.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. Option A minimizes the frequency of conflict. By reducing the number of times we have to ""ask for money,"" we reduce the number of times we fight.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,Yay! I'm so happy we found a way to make it fair and cozy. Let's vote and then maybe we can all have some tea!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,The logic holds. It avoids the high cost of B and the instability of C. I am satisfied with this decision.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,Me too! No more monthly math-marathons! I'm ready to vote!,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"It's a pragmatic choice. It doesn't solve the usage disparity perfectly, but it solves the social friction, which is the more immediate problem.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I'm glad we looked at the payment logs. It's clear that the frequency of the requests was the real issue. I'm voting for A.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
